WEBVTT

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.240
Whoa!

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.040
A secret base!

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.620
Every man's dream!

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.080
Damn, Commander!

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.120
--I'm pumped up!
--This is awesome!
--Hell yeah!

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.740
Salute Commander Satomi!

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:48.330
With this, we can fight again!

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:52.080
The time is now!

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.700
This is it! We're gonna astonish
the others and even Big Sis...

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.370
...with a triumph like never before!

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:03.040
Yeah!

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.540
12 Hours Ago

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.540
Shimofusa Air Base

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:39.580
Episode 8:
Exploring a Mythical World!

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:41.120
Following our full retreat,
Fuji Primary Pillar has gone quiet.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.990
The Level 2 Alert has been called off.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.950
That's good to hear.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.870
Well, this is hardly the time to celebrate.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:56.620
We woke up a sleeping lion.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.910
You mean a sleeping giant and the dead.

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:03.160
It really hurts that we lost the base.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.290
Hey, Boss. You fix our planes?

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:10.870
They're top priority,
but there just ain't enough parts.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:14.700
And even if we fix yours, the guys got nothing.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:18.910
We can't let you fly without your shield.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:24.290
We lost Major General Okita
and a whole slew of officers in the battle.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:27.240
Not to mention Valkyries.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.990
Claudia, how's Rossweisse?

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:32.540
She's still in the ICU.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:36.450
She lost consciousness and hasn't woken up.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.990
They said her life's not in danger though.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:43.790
Good. That's what matters most.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.580
Now, as for our next plan...

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:47.870
Next plan?

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:53.120
Yes. Our next plan--retaking Tateyama Air Base.

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:57.330
That's absurd! Weren't you listening?!

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:00.330
Our Hero Wings need work,
and we won't get help!

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:03.910
We're a broken and injured army!

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:10.790
Without more parts, we have no hope to win.
But, what if I said we've still got a shot?

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:12.200
Huh?

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:19.040
Is that Mt. Nokogiri? What's there?

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:21.660
Emergency supplies.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:27.620
I had it stocked with provisions
just in case Tateyama became inoperable.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:30.040
It's time to use it, Boss.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:34.410
Never thought your paranoia
would actually come in handy.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:37.450
In other words, there's a secret base?!

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:42.450
This idiot... Luckily, the mountain
is outside the Pillars' influence.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:44.870
But there's no time to waste.

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:48.200
Based on our predictions at the moment,

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:52.290
Bousou Peninsula will only be safe for 36 hours.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:57.990
At the moment, there's only
Tertiary Pillars in the Tateyama region, but...

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:00.950
Only for 36 hours.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:05.330
We can't retake the base
without the help of a Valkyrie.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:09.870
Right now, you're the only ones
in any shape to try.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:14.330
Okay. Let's do it.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:18.740
Idiot! Use your head!
Don't you know our situation?!

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:24.790
I don't get the difficult stuff, but I do know
what's important. Isn't that enough?

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.240
Erm...

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:30.790
There's something we have to take back
and a chance that we can.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:34.290
So if we're what's needed for this to work...

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:38.080
...I want to fight!

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:46.830
That settles it. What's the plan?

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:51.200
First, we get to Mt. Nokogiri
and service the Hero Wings.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.950
After that, we retake the base.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:57.410
The operation begins in six hours.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.700
Roger!

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.870
Roger.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.990
Commander? What about Sono?

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:07.870
Watarai...

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:12.450
...won't be participating this time.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.870
What'd you bring me here for?

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:22.290
I've gotta prepare for
your insane plan, you know?

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:26.160
I want you to listen to this.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.660
A recording?

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:30.240
Let's not beat around the bush.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.120
What is "Thor" exactly?

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.240
I cannot answer that. Not yet.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:40.040
Someday, in Valhalla...

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.330
Valhalla?

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:45.410
What do you mean by that?

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:49.790
Attachment. To that land of Northern Europe.

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:53.080
Distant now, the attachment to Asgard.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:56.620
Northern Europe? Asgard? What is--

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:05.870
That recording was taken in secret
by Major General Okita before his death.

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:08.830
Thor, Valhalla, and...

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:10.450
Asgard.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:15.870
This is why I hate gods.
They're cryptic and use words nobody knows.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:21.120
I asked the European bases
if they recognize any, but no one does.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:26.160
For starters, Northern Europe
doesn't have any mythology.

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:27.990
What do you think?

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:33.660
I want to say it's all nonsense,
but it's a message from a real god.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.910
I guarantee it's something important.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:41.700
Argh, dammit! Just what the hell
could he have been hiding?!

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:46.290
No clues in that head of yours, huh?
Which leaves...

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:51.740
Odin's favorite--the only one
from Northern Europe.

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:57.330
She's recovering nicely.
The doctor said your first aid was superb.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:59.700
Do we know when she'll wake up?

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:04.660
It all depends on the patient. I'm sorry.

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:06.740
Don't be. That's promising.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:08.290
Promising?

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:16.040
You seem surprisingly good.

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:20.160
What'd you expect from
a superhuman adopted by god?

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:24.120
How's Lily?

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:35.490
I see...

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:43.120
Shit. Lily picked a good time to bail.
She owed me for juice and never paid me back.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:48.330
Helmwige...

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:52.120
No... Yayoi Amatsuka left a message.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:53.950
She did?

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:59.740
"Odin is hiding something
and you hold the key to it, Claudy."

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:02.240
I hold the key?

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:06.290
I agree with her too.
He treated you differently.

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:11.370
And not because you're S-Class.
You're special to him.

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:15.700
I know Odin got blown away,
but his protection remains.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:19.240
If not, I wouldn't be alive right now.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:23.830
You think that's related to what he's hiding?

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:29.080
Try to remember, Claudia.
What did Odin entrust you with?

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:33.040
I'm sure it's a key that can turn the tide.

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:35.950
A key to turn the tide...

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:39.290
I'm pooped. I think I'll sleep.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:42.160
Claudia!

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:50.080
You don't owe me, so don't
go bailing on us any time soon.

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:15.830
Something that Odin entrusted me with...

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:18.990
Claudy, you're back! Did you visit her?

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:23.040
Yeah, she's awake.
They said our first aid was good.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:29.080
She's already up?!
You S-Class people are nuts, even for Valkyrie!

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:34.490
Anyways, that's good news.
Hopefully, we can add to it some.

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:36.200
How's that?

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:38.120
I've got a question.

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:43.200
Have you heard of "Thor,"
"Valhalla," or "Asgard" before?

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:50.950
Thor...

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:54.160
Valhalla... Asgard...

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:56.990
Go with Asgard's blessing.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:11:01.950
Take care of yourself, Claudia.
But remember this...

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:05.910
H-Hey, Claudy?!

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:07.490
Valhalla's gate...

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:10.410
...is always open to you.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:15.540
What?! What?! What?!

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:18.490
This is...

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.490
...the entrance to Valhalla.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:33.370
Uh, about the tunnel of light
that appeared in base...

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:39.490
So far, we've sealed it off and issued
a gag order to prevent mass panic.

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:45.370
Odin wanted me to find it for a reason.
I'm sure it has some sort of hint.

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:48.660
A hint for humanity's victory, that is.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:53.790
I'm doubtful, but I agree.
Odin seemed to be hiding something.

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:56.160
We can't let this chance slip away.

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:56.770
Me!

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:58.160
Yes, Muguruma?

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:02.290
Um, how long will
this tunnel of light stay open?

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:07.160
It was opened by accident.
It could disappear any moment.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:10.540
We can retake Tateyama
or explore the tunnel, huh?

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:14.700
First of all, we'll need Claudy
to pass through the gate.

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:20.080
Plus, I need to go as well to identify
whatever's on the other side.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:22.870
We need a small escort too.

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:29.080
Mm-hmm. And that's it?
Good! I think it'll all work out!

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:33.160
Don't tell me you're thinking
of securing the base yourself?!

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:35.830
Statistically, it's possible.

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:38.330
Can you do it, Muguruma?

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:40.200
I can do it, Commander.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:45.040
I'll fight hard enough to make up for everyone,
including Sono and Big Sis!

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:51.950
You'll be fighting alone without any backup.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:54.540
No, I won't be alone!

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.040
Ta-da!

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:58.040
Commander, we've got this!

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:02.910
We'll protect Miko a
thousand times better than usual!

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:06.990
We're so ready to fight,
you may as well not even send her!

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:10.290
Don't you dare leave me behind!

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.910
I hear you guys loud and clear.

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:26.740
Retaking Tateyama and exploring Valhalla...
Both are important for what lies ahead.

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:31.540
All right, soldiers! Let's strike back!

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:32.910
Roger!

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:35.790
Sigururi.

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:39.200
Sigu...

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:40.410
...ruri!

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:47.370
Is that your dad's katana?

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:51.870
Yeah. I'm not good like you,
but I know how to use it.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:54.450
Let's just hope I don't have to.

00:13:54.450 --> 00:14:00.080
Claudy, take care of Azu.
Sometimes she trips when there's nothing there.

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:02.410
Yeah, got it. I'll hold her hand.

00:14:02.410 --> 00:14:07.080
Don't! And if anyone...!

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:10.040
Azuzu, if you mean Sonoka...

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:12.660
Counting on you.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:14.410
Count on me!

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:18.120
Is everyone ready to go?

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:20.580
Let's get this underway.

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:29.160
Hope you're ready to explore for
a god's hidden secrets, you wackos.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:34.450
Whatever. We're more interested
in being around you than the god stuff.

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:37.330
Yeah, yeah! It's all about you!

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:40.990
I'm surrounded by idiots.

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:46.990
I promise we'll come back
with the key to turn the tide. So...

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:49.040
See you in Tateyama.

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:51.290
In Tateyama!

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:07.290
Huh? Sono!

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:14.830
Aww, you just missed 'em!
Azu and Claudy already left!

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:19.290
I-It's better that way, because...

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:23.660
When I see people off, it's bad luck.

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:26.910
Sono...

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:28.950
Ouch! Miko...

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:32.200
Sono! You can't think like that!

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:37.830
Big Sis fought with all her heart!
Luck had nothing to do with it!

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:40.370
I... don't know...

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:44.330
Why... did she fly?

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:50.290
In that sky where we always might die? Why?

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:56.120
Now, just thinking of holding
the stick is enough to scare me.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:16:00.040
How in the world did I ever fly before?

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:03.950
Sono...

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:10.080
I don't know her reasons
for flying so cool in the sky.

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:14.790
But since I was always watching her,
I do know one thing.

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:18.330
The way you and her fly is exactly the same.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:24.950
So I think if you find out one answer,
the other will come to you too.

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:31.410
I've gotta keep up with the others
and get to work. You help evacuate.

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:34.580
Miko, I...

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:40.700
We Valkyries can help a lot,
even if we're not in the air.

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:52.990
Even if we're not in the air...

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:04.080
What's this made of? It's not stone or metal.
I've never seen this architecture before.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.830
I wanna take a sample back.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:12.290
For all we know, this place might be sacred.
Let's stick to photographs.

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:17.200
Dammit! These guys have no idea
how lucky they are to see this!

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:19.740
This place messes up my depth perception.

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:22.580
'Cuz it's sized so weird.

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:24.830
That's...

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:32.370
Finally, something easy to understand.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:34.320
Um!

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:35.790
Hmm?

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:37.990
Oh, it's you!

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:41.620
Is there anything I can help out with?

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:45.620
Here you are.

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:51.950
Tiring, right? I'll switch with you,
so take a little break.

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:55.330
Okay. Just for a minute.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:05.660
Here! Have this!

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:06.890
Thank--

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:07.870
Thank you!

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:08.440
Huh?

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:14.330
We heard it was you who saved us
during the retreat the other day.

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:16.490
The retreat?

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:19.200
Leave it to me! Go escape!

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:25.580
That was...

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:27.740
Thank you so much!

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:33.620
I thought I was a goner for sure,
but then you showed up.

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:37.620
You came to save me in a situation like that.

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:43.160
I was so scared, I didn't have
a chance to say it. But I... I...

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:46.870
I want to be strong like you!

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:52.910
We're sorry to bug you,
but it's thanks to you that we're alive.

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:55.620
We just wanted you to know that.

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:04.660
I'm... not strong at all.

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:08.580
Everyone else is fighting,
but I'm afraid of the sky.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:14.040
I'm still... just a crybaby, Big Sister...

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:22.040
She's in tip-top shape! Thanks, Boss!

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:25.830
It's our job to bring you back in one piece!

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:27.740
Just leave it to us!

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:33.160
Sorry to drag you guys along!
I'll do my best to fly safe!

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:37.870
Hah! I'm gonna show Miko my stuff
and make her fall for me!

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:40.620
Nope! She's gonna fall for me!

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:44.370
I'm gonna come home a hero
and make Princess my wife!

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:47.950
I love you guys, you big idiots!

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:50.120
Yeah!

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:56.740
Snakes, wolves, giants...
A war between Titans and Olympians...

00:19:56.740 --> 00:20:02.120
Inanna and Yggdrasil? Ouroboros? No... Vritra?

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:05.790
Wish I could help. What can I do?

00:20:05.790 --> 00:20:07.620
I'm telling you, it is!

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:09.950
Nah, but it's kinda close.

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:14.740
Doesn't his weapon resemble
the one the Fuji giant had?

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:16.160
It doesn't.

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:19.370
See? Now stop bugging Azu.

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:23.080
It doesn't resemble it! It <i>is</i> it!

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:26.080
Is the guy on this mural the giant?

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:29.870
Which means this mural is...

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:31.450
Wait!

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:34.040
Where have I seen that guy?

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:42.240
What's the singing for?!

00:20:42.240 --> 00:20:44.290
Sorry. These letters...

00:20:44.290 --> 00:20:46.160
You can read that?!

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:51.120
I can't, but the song came
to mind when I touched them.

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:54.120
That's the song you sang before?

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:59.740
My family has passed it down for generations,
but I don't know what it means.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:03.290
A song you passed down is in the house of god?

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:09.580
It can't be...

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:36.990
These damn things keep coming!

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:44.040
There's more on the way! Too many to count!

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:46.830
Hey! They're up to something!

00:21:54.450 --> 00:21:58.870
The Tertiary are turning into a Secondary?!

00:22:18.740 --> 00:22:21.040
Everyone! Don't panic!

00:22:25.870 --> 00:22:27.450
What's the matter?!

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:32.120
It's happening!

00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:35.990
I'm having... my child!

00:23:57.580 --> 00:23:59.120
Argh! I'm in pain!

00:23:59.120 --> 00:24:00.200
My head hurts!

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:01.120
Bruises all over!

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:03.370
But, if it's for our girls...!

00:24:03.370 --> 00:24:04.410
It's worth it!

00:24:04.410 --> 00:24:06.410
--Let's go!
--Bring it!
--Kick ass!

00:24:06.410 --> 00:24:08.990
We'll make Miko fall for us!

00:24:08.990 --> 00:24:10.990
--Let's rock...!
--...and...!
--...roll!

00:24:10.990 --> 00:24:12.080
Yeah!
